      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The borough’s glassmaking heritage began in 1806 when Irish immigrant James Lee opened the first factory, using local silica sand and wood.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Millville%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Levoy Theatre, opened in 1908, closed for 34 years before reopening in 2012 with silent films and a live orchestra.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Millville%2C_New_Jersey",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Millville’s Glasstown Arts District preserves the legacy of the historic Millville Glass Works, now a cultural hub.",
